"Let $G$ be a graph, and let $(a,b)$-choosability mean that every assignment of lists of size $a$ to the vertices of $G$ admits a coloring in which each vertex receives a color from its list and each color is used on at most $b$ vertices. **Erdős–Rubin–Taylor conjecture.** If $G$ is $(a,b)$-choosable, then $G$ is $(an,bn)$-choosable for every $n\\in\\mathbb{N}$. A positive answer to part (i) of Problem 1 would follow from this conjecture; its resolution is not specified in the source."